# A job run in one of two modes. Each choice is made once, in a place with a name: where the job comes from is the
# body of `source`, a choice between `load` and `infer` whose Job either arm makes; `report` builds its Message by one
# constructor in either arm, the level's own method marking it. The settings are the route's own value: a call
# handed `settings.mode` or `settings.level` is handed the settings, the projection glued into the call; inside, the
# parameter that holds the field is the value its steps take.

route runs.core.run
step run/source
choice run/source/?1
step run/source/?1/load
step run/source/?1/load/Job()
step run/source/?1/infer
step run/source/?1/infer/Job()
step run/finished
step run/finished/Runner()
step run/finished/Runner.batch
step run/report
choice run/report/?1
step run/report/?1/Level.prefix
step run/report/?1/Message()
step run/report/?1/Level.suffix
step run/report/?1/Message()#2
step run/report/send

line entry > run call
line Settings·settings > run value                                 # run reads the mode and the level from it

# where the job comes from
line run/source/?1/load/Job() > Job@run/source/?1/load/Job() value
line Job@run/source/?1/load/Job() > run/source/?1/load value
line run/source/?1/load > Job@run/source/?1 value
line run/source/?1/infer/Job() > Job@run/source/?1/infer/Job() value
line Job@run/source/?1/infer/Job() > run/source/?1/infer value
line run/source/?1/infer > Job@run/source/?1 value
line Job@run/source/?1 > run/source value                          # source hands back the Job either arm made
line run/source > Job·job@run/source value
line Job·job@run/source > run/finished value                       # finished counts its steps
line Job·job@run/source > run/report/?1/Message() value             # each Message writes its name
line Job·job@run/source > run/report/?1/Message()#2 value

# whether it finished: a Runner for the mode, and the mode's timeout
line Settings·settings > run/finished value                       # finished looks up the mode's plan itself
line Mode·mode > run/finished/Runner() value
line run/finished/Runner() > Runner@run/finished/Runner() value
line Runner@run/finished/Runner() > run/finished/Runner.batch value
line run/finished/Runner.batch > run/finished back
line run/finished > _@run/finished value                           # the bool, handed straight to report
line _@run/finished > run/report value
line Settings·settings > run/report value                         # its level, held by report's `level`

# the line that says how it went: what the level's method gives goes into the Message built around it
line Level·level > run/report/?1/Level.prefix value
line Level·level > run/report/?1/Level.suffix value
line run/report/?1/Level.prefix > _@run/report/?1 value
line _@run/report/?1 > run/report/?1/Message() value
line run/report/?1/Level.suffix > _@run/report/?1#2 value
line _@run/report/?1#2 > run/report/?1/Message()#2 value
line run/report/?1/Message() > Message·message@run/report/?1 value
line run/report/?1/Message()#2 > Message·message@run/report/?1 value
line Message·message@run/report/?1 > run/report/send value
line run/report/send > Screen own
line run/report/send > run/report back
line run/report > run back

home Settings·settings run
home Mode·mode run
home Level·level run
home Job@run/source/?1/load/Job() run/source/?1/load
home Job@run/source/?1/infer/Job() run/source/?1/infer
home Job@run/source/?1 run/source
home Job·job@run/source run
home Runner@run/finished/Runner() run/finished
home _@run/finished run
home _@run/report/?1 run/report/?1
home _@run/report/?1#2 run/report/?1
home Message·message@run/report/?1 run/report

side entry left
side Screen right

# an opened step's own arrow takes what its steps make, or what its call is handed, though only a step inside takes it
known #new extra line Job·job@run/source > run/report value
known #new extra line Job·job@run/source > run value
known #new extra line Runner@run/finished/Runner() > run/finished value
known #new extra line Message·message@run/report/?1 > run/report value

# a result of no type of the code's handed straight to another step goes back to the caller as well
known #new extra line run/finished > run back
known #new extra line run/report/?1/Level.prefix > run/report back
known #new extra line run/report/?1/Level.suffix > run/report back
